// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`setupPromptOf: the fixtures > the agent team 1`] = `
"Use Hermes Agent.

Model: Opus 5.5.

Add the skill release-notes.
Install the skill email-triage from ClawHub.

Create a shared notes folder of markdown files in Obsidian, synced with git, that the agents read. Add these notes:

voice: How the business writes.
\`\`\`
Short sentences. No jargon.
\`\`\`

clients: Who we work for.
\`\`\`
{client_name} pays monthly.
\`\`\`

Give Researcher persistent memory in Mem0, kept in the cloud.
Tag each memory with the agent that saved it, and review entries after 90 days.
Give Writer persistent memory in Mem0, kept in the cloud.
Tag each memory with the agent that saved it.
Give Reviewer persistent memory in Mem0, kept in the cloud.
Tag each memory with the agent that saved it.
Let the agents reach each other through a relay on Tailscale that queues messages while an agent is offline.

Keep working towards this goal: Keep the launch post on track.

Have an AI reviewer check each action, and ask a person when it is unsure (reviewer model: Haiku 5.5).
Run commands in a container.

Create three agents that talk in one group chat.

Give every agent these team instructions:

\`\`\`
Write in plain English for {audience}. Keep every source in the shared notes, and say when you are unsure.
\`\`\`

Researcher: Find three sources for each claim. Hands off to Writer when three sources are found. Model: Opus 5.5. Connect Slack (read and write), GitHub (read and write) and Gmail (read only).
Writer: Write the post from the sources, then ask @Reviewer to check it. Hands off to Reviewer when the draft is complete. Model: Sonnet 5.5. Connect Slack (read and write), GitHub (read and write) and Gmail (read only).
Reviewer: Check the draft against the sources. Hands off to Writer when changes are needed. Model: Qwen2.5. Connect Slack (read and write), GitHub (read and write) and Gmail (read only).

Give each agent its own git worktree, and have Reviewer merge one change at a time.

For example:
Researcher found three sources on the launch and passed on a source list.
Writer wrote the first draft and passed on the draft.
Reviewer asked for a shorter opening and passed on two changes.
Writer made the changes and passed on the final draft.

Replace {client_name} before running.
Replace {audience} before running."
`;

exports[`setupPromptOf: the fixtures > the assistant 1`] = `
"Use OpenClaw on an always-on machine (Mac Mini).

Model: Opus 5.5. The maker reports it also works with GPT and Gemini.

Give it these instructions:

\`\`\`
You are {your_name}'s assistant.
\`\`\`

Create AGENTS.md with this content:

\`\`\`
I am {your_name}. I run {your_business} for {your_clients}.
\`\`\`

Add the skill inbox-zero: sorts the inbox.
Add the skill meeting-prep.
Add the skill weekly-review.

Add the MCP server gmail. It needs \${GMAIL_TOKEN}.
Add the MCP server google-calendar. It needs \${GOOGLE_TOKEN}.

Connect Gmail and Google Calendar.

Give it persistent memory in Letta, kept in the cloud.
Receive and send messages on Telegram. It needs \${TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN}.
Receive and send messages on WhatsApp. It needs \${WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN}.
Speak replies with ElevenLabs (text-to-speech).
Give it a front end built with Claude Design.

Run it all the time as a background service, listening for messages on Telegram and WhatsApp.

Replace {your_name} (your first name) before running.
Replace {your_business} (your business) before running.
Replace {your_clients} (who you work for) before running."
`;

exports[`setupPromptOf: the fixtures > the chief of staff 1`] = `
"Use Claude Code.

Model: Opus 5.5.

Create a shared notes folder of markdown files in Obsidian, synced with git, that every agent reads. Add these notes:

voice: How the agency writes.
\`\`\`
Short sentences. Name the next step. Sign off as {sender_name}.
\`\`\`

clients: Who the agency works for.
\`\`\`
{client_name}: what they buy, who decides, when they last heard from us.
\`\`\`

pipeline: Deals in progress.
\`\`\`
{deal_name}, worth {deal_value}, next step on {next_date}.
\`\`\`

Give the agents persistent memory in Mem0, kept in the cloud.
Tag each memory with the agent that saved it, and review entries after 90 days.
Let the agents reach each other through a relay on Tailscale that queues messages while an agent is offline.
Receive and send messages on Slack. It needs \${SLACK_BOT_TOKEN}.

Run it when a request arrives in Slack.

Ask before risky actions.
Run commands in a container.

Create four agents led by the first, who hands work to the others.

Give every agent these team instructions:

\`\`\`
The Chief of staff reads each request and passes it to one specialist: market questions to @Research, client emails to @Sales, and sheets or schedules to @Operations. Every agent writes for {agency_name} and keeps its notes in the shared folder.
\`\`\`

Chief of staff: Read each request, decide who does it, and say back who has it. Hands off to Research when it needs research. Hands off to Sales when it needs a client email. Hands off to Operations when it needs a sheet updated. Model: Opus 5.5.
Research: Find what the request needs from the inbox and the web, and cite where each fact came from. Hands off to Operations when a deal needs adding to the pipeline. Model: Sonnet 5.5. Connect Gmail (read only).
Operations: Keep the pipeline sheet and the team's schedule up to date. Model: Haiku 5.5. Connect Slack (read and write) and Google Sheets (read and write).
Sales: Draft replies to clients in the agency's voice. Model: Sonnet 5.5. Connect Gmail (read and write).

Research, job 2: Weekly market report. Deliver a report named Weekly market report to Google Drive, Research folder.

\`\`\`
Write this week's market report for {agency_name}.
\`\`\`

Operations, job 2: Pipeline sheet. Deliver a sheet named Weekly pipeline sheet to Google Sheets.

\`\`\`
Update the pipeline sheet with this week's deals.
\`\`\`

Sales: For everything you produce: drafts only, never send; one question per email.

Sales: Follow this guidance: Plain English guide (https://www.plainenglish.example/guide).

Sales, job 2: Client follow-up. Deliver a draft named Client follow-up email to Gmail. Wait for approval before delivering it.

\`\`\`
Draft a follow-up to {client_name} about the proposal.
\`\`\`

For example:
Chief of staff read a request for a client follow-up and passed on the request.
Research pulled the client's last three emails and passed on a short brief.
Sales drafted the follow-up email and passed on the draft.
Research found the open deal in the inbox and passed on the deal details.
Operations added the deal to the pipeline sheet and passed on the updated sheet.

Research reads outside content and passes work to Operations, which can send. Add an approval between them before running.

Replace {sender_name} before running.
Replace {client_name} before running.
Replace {deal_name} before running.
Replace {deal_value} before running.
Replace {next_date} before running.
Replace {agency_name} before running."
`;

exports[`setupPromptOf: the fixtures > the self-hosted team 1`] = `
"Build it in code with LangGraph on an always-on machine (Workstation).

Model: Qwen2.5 32B, Q4_K_M, GGUF, served by Ollama (OpenAI-compatible API).

Watch it with Grafana (tokens per second, latency and GPU use).
Charge the agent's users through Stripe, usage-based per 1M tokens.

Create two agents that hand work to each other.

Triage. Model: Qwen2.5.
Resolver. Model: Qwen2.5."
`;
